\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{3dfe909}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Three additions to inference, published off. \code{\verb~|pchk~} shares check facts: a closed export term without level parameters that passed check mode is inferred without being checked again by later declarations and workers, never after an eager-reduction comparison. \code{\verb~|match~} matches a telescope domain against the inferred type of the argument instead of building the domain, and falls through to the complete procedure when it cannot tell. \code{\verb~|joint~} checks the telescopes of a declaration's type and value together. Instruction counts, which repeat exactly, with all three on top of \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} (native image, one worker): Init 105.6 to 101.7 G (-3.7 \%), Std 177.9 to 170.2 G (-4.3 \%), Cedar slice 39.6 to 39.0 G (-1.5 \%), reachability 59.1 to 59.0 G. On 9,110 tutorial mutants there was no soundness and no completeness difference. All three joined the default set at the integration of wave 6.}

\p{Detail: [design-switches-document](design-switches-document), [rep-machine-M5](rep-machine-M5). Commit \commit{3dfe909}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE). Related: [the inference shortcuts](design-inference-shortcuts), [the switches](design-switches).}
